eb.archive.org/web/20210831045447/https://looksmax.org/threads/the-looksmaxxers-guide-to-retin-a-tretinoin-skinmaxxers-acnecels-gtfih.6107/"},{"title":"gunna buy retin a","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/gunna-buy-retin-a.3495/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230528140551/https://looksmax.org/threads/gunna-buy-retin-a.3495/"}],"news":[],"social":[{"title":"Netflix buffering issues: Boxing fans complain about Jake Paul vs. Mike Tyson","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=42153953","site":"Hacker News","score":492,"comments":924,"year":2024},{"title":"Why pipes sometimes get \"stuck\": buffering","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=42275033","site":"Hacker News","score":391,"comments":103,"year":2024},{"title":"Why is Netflix Buffering? Dispelling the Congestion Myth","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=8016055","site":"Hacker News","score":106,"comments":213,"year":2014},{"title":"Show HN: OpenGL in super slow motion – visualising Z-buffering","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=12030172","site":"Hacker News","score":276,"comments":38,"year":2016},{"title":"'Green roads' are plowing ahead, buffering drought and floods","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=38654432","site":"Hacker News","score":101,"comments":53,"year":2023},{"title":"Disk write buffering and its interactions with write flushes","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=39741096","site":"Hacker News","score":76,"comments":58,"year":2024},{"title":"Google Fiber: Working with content providers to minimize buffering","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=7784687","site":"Hacker News","score":79,"comments":24,"year":2014},{"title":"Gnome / mutter triple buffering patch merged","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=43371781","site":"Hacker News","score":74,"comments":25,"year":2025},{"title":"Grid scale buffering with molten salt batteries that run at 500 Celsius","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=34914779","site":"Hacker News","score":56,"comments":19,"year":2023},{"title":"Double Buffering with Cloudflare Queues","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50276613","site":"Hacker News","score":57,"comments":8,"year":2026},{"title":"TTY and Buffering","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=46659635","site":"Hacker News","score":46,"comments":17,"year":2026},{"title":"UART Receive Buffering","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=9700868","site":"Hacker News","score":41,"comments":14,"year":2015},{"title":"Triple Buffering in Rendering APIs","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=45313180","site":"Hacker News","score":43,"comments":3,"year":2025},{"title":"Event Buffering","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=3712042","site":"Hacker News","score":34,"comments":8,"year":2012},{"title":"How input buffering works [video]","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=39656002","site":"Hacker News","score":21,"comments":0,"year":2024}],"web":[{"title":"Tretinoin","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tretinoin"},{"title":"Wrinkle","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wrinkle"},{"title":"Retinoid","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Retinoid"}]},"angle":{"goal":"Anti-aging","effect":"indirect","chain":["Retinoid speeds skin cell turnover","Collagen builds, pores and spots improve","Smoother, clearer, younger-looking skin"],"text":"Looksmaxxing forums share routines for starting tretinoin slowly and buffering it with moisturiser to reduce irritation, aiming for smoother, clearer, less wrinkled skin. The retinoid speeds skin cell turnover and builds collagen. Tretinoin itself has been studied for acne and photoaging for up to two years."},"wikipedia":null,"grokipedia":null,"lead":["The tretinoin protocol, often shortened to \"tret\" in forums, refers to the way looksmaxxing practitioners introduce and use topical tretinoin, a prescription retinoid, typically by increasing use slowly and sometimes \"buffering\" it with moisturiser to reduce irritation.","Topical tretinoin is described as the most extensively studied retinoid for photoageing, and studies have run up to two years.[1] Its common adverse effects are irritation, redness, peeling and sun sensitivity.[1] Reference sources do not describe buffering or slow-ramp schedules specifically, so those practices rest on community and clinician convention rather than the sources reviewed here."],"infobox":[["Drug class","Retinoid (first generation)"],["Route","Topical"],["Brand names","Retin-A, Avita, Renova"],["Approved for acne (US)","1971"],["Pregnancy","Contraindicated"]],"sections":[{"h":"Description","paras":["Tretinoin is all-trans retinoic acid. Topical forms are used for acne and for photoaged skin.[1] Practitioners in appearance communities describe starting at low frequency, increasing gradually as the skin adapts, and applying a moisturiser before or after the product (buffering) to moderate irritation. These are descriptions of community practice, not dosing instructions."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Effects and adverse effects","paras":["Wikipedia reports that tretinoin may increase collagen production and that visible improvement in photoageing typically takes weeks to months.[1] Topical use commonly causes skin irritation, redness, swelling and peeling and may increase sun sensitivity.[1]","Tretinoin is contraindicated in pregnancy because of the risk of birth defects; Australia rates topical tretinoin category D.[1] The American Academy of Dermatology is quoted as saying retinoids should not be used during pregnancy.[2] Among cosmetic wrinkle treatments, tretinoin and tazarotene are described as the only topical retinoids approved for photodamage wrinkles.[3]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"History","paras":["Tretinoin was patented in 1957 and approved for medical use in 1962; Albert Kligman and colleagues at the University of Pennsylvania developed its acne use, and the FDA approved it for acne in 1971.[1] Retin-A Micro, a microsphere gel, was approved in 1997.[1]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["Controlled studies of topical tretinoin for photoageing have been published, with durations up to two years.[1] No studies were found that specifically compare buffering or slow-ramp schedules."],"subs":[]}],"lore":null,"timeline":[{"year":"1957","event":"Tretinoin patented.[1]"},{"year":"1962","event":"Approved for medical use.[1]"},{"year":"1971","event":"FDA approves tretinoin for acne.[1]"},{"year":"1997","event":"Retin-A Micro approved.[1]"}],"refs":[{"title":"Tretinoin","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tretinoin","source":"Wikipedia","year":2026,"type":"encyclopedia"},{"title":"Retinoid","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Retinoid","source":"Wikipedia","year":2026,"type":"encyclopedia"},{"title":"Wrinkle","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wrinkle","source":"Wikipedia","year":2026,"type":"encyclopedia"}],"studies":[{"title":"Tretinoin","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tretinoin","source":"Wikipedia","year":2026,"kind":null}],"reddit":[],"forums":[{"title":"Discussion Retin-A on eyelids: risk of getting MGD or dry/red eyes?","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/retin-a-on-eyelids-risk-of-getting-mgd-or-dry-red-eyes.572036/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20220920180953/https://looksmax.org/threads/retin-a-on-eyelids-risk-of-getting-mgd-or-dry-red-eyes.572036/"},{"title":"LifeFuel Retin A does burn fat on the face","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/retin-a-does-burn-fat-on-the-face.495707/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20220513134223/https://looksmax.org/threads/retin-a-does-burn-fat-on-the-face.495707/"},{"title":"retin a since 22 and dutasteride + dermarolling since 25 (28 now)","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/retin-a-since-22-and-dutasteride-dermarolling-since-25-28-now.433290/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20211218203007/https://looksmax.org/threads/retin-a-since-22-and-dutasteride-dermarolling-since-25-28-now